.TH CHTTPSVR_REQ_QUERY_OOM 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_req_query_oom \- check whether chttpsvr_req_query ran out of memory
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpserver.h>

bool chttpsvr_req_query_oom(const chttpsvr_req *req);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Returns true when an allocation for the query string of this request
failed because the library ran out of memory.  Two allocations can
fail this way: growing the result array inside chttpsvr_req_query,
and the one-time, shared parse of the query string, which
chttpsvr_req_query and chttpsvr_req_query_one each start lazily on
first use.

chttpsvr_req_query returns NULL and a count of 0 both when the
requested key is absent and when a lack of memory stopped it from
building the result array; after any NULL return from
chttpsvr_req_query, use this function to tell the two cases apart.

The flag latches: once set, it stays true for the rest of the request,
whatever query calls follow.  This function returns false when req is
NULL.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
true; an allocation for the query string of this request failed out of
memory.
false; no allocation error happened, or req is NULL.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_req_query (3),
.BR chttpsvr_req_query_one (3)
